Description: Stream your Linux desktop to a Smart TV
 FluxCast mirrors a Linux desktop to a Smart TV over Miracast/Wi-Fi Display,
 DLNA, or Chromecast, with a system tray applet and a command line interface.
 .
 Wi-Fi Display is the primary path: screen and audio capture are encoded to
 H.264/AAC and carried over a Wi-Fi Direct link negotiated through
 NetworkManager or wpa_supplicant, with RTSP session control.
 .
 The Python dependencies that the archive does not carry at a usable version
 (python3-upnpclient is absent, python3-pychromecast is too old) ship in a
 private virtualenv under /opt/fluxcast rather than as system packages. That
 virtualenv is tied to the Python version this package was built against, so
 the dependency on python3 is pinned to a single minor version.
